## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to implement a minimal retrieval loop that works with embeddings, chunking, and a vector-like store, while considering multilingual routing and update freshness.

## Key Concepts

- In-memory vector store
- Text chunking with overlap
- Embedding generation
- Cosine similarity search
- Multilingual handling
- Update freshness and caching

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo JS snippet: minimal in-memory index
const model = loadModel('all-MiniLM-L6-v2');
function chunk(text, max=300, overlap=50){ /* split and overlap */ }
let index = [];
function indexDocs(docs){
  docs.forEach(doc=>{
    chunk(doc.text).forEach(ch=>{
      index.push({id: doc.id+':' + hash(ch), text: ch, emb: model.encode(ch)});
    });
  });
}
function query(q, topK=5){
  const qEmb = model.encode(q);
  return index
    .map(n => ({...n, score: cosine(n.emb, qEmb)}))
    .sort((a,b)=> b.score-a.score)
    .slice(0, topK);
}
```

